<title>GERMANY: Bayer not considering cloned animals for research.</title>
<headline>Bayer not considering cloned animals for research.</headline>
<dateline>LEVERKUSEN, Germany 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>German chemicals group Bayer AG said it was not considering whether cells from cloned animals should be used for testing of human medicines.</p>
<p>Peter Stadtler, the director of Bayer's biotechnology division, also told journalists at a company event late on Wednesday that Bayer had no interest in developing ways to change gene technology in humans.</p>
<p>The issue of genetic experiments has come to the forefront after British scientists unveiled a sheep who had been cloned by using the cell of an adult sheep.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
